UPDATE companies SET description='Southwestern Wire is headquartered in Norman, Oklahoma, and traces its origins to March 1992 when Max Moore and Steve Peters acquired the machinery and equipment of Acme Fence and Iron from the Bank of Oklahoma. The founders spent the first year rebuilding and modernizing the plant, installing a state‑of‑the‑art wire galvanizing line that enabled heavier zinc coatings up to 1.2 oz./sq. ft. and positioned the company to compete with larger domestic and foreign wire manufacturers.

The company manufactures a broad range of wire and fence products: galvanized and vinyl‑coated chain link fence fabric (including preslatted and security mini‑mesh up to 20 ft tall), fabricated panel products such as residential bent‑frame gates, dog kennels and temporary fence panels, agricultural wire (vineyard, trellis, high‑tensile and electric fence wire), industrial low‑ and high‑carbon wire (C1006–C1026 and 1027–1065), recycling wire (single‑loop bale ties in black annealed and galvanized finishes), and galvanized tension bars, truss rods, drop rods and gate rods. Southwestern Wire owns and operates three manufacturing facilities in the United States — Norman, OK; Birmingham, AL; and Sacramento, CA — with a major 30,000 sq. ft. expansion added in 1998.

Primary customers are expert distributors in each product category. The company serves the chain link fence industry, industrial wire users, recycling and baling operations, high‑carbon wire markets, agricultural sectors (vineyards, cattle grazing), and security/prison construction where its mini‑mesh products are specified.

Southwestern Wire emphasizes domestic production — "products melted and manufactured in the United States of America" — and points to its 1993 establishment of the only mass‑production galvanized tension bar facility in the U.S. as a key differentiator. The ability to apply Class 5 galvanizing (2 oz./sq. ft.) meeting ASTM A392 Class 2, along with ongoing investments in technology and employee development, underpins its "Made In The USA" positioning.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Hot\u2011dip galvanizing (Class 5, up to 2 oz./ft\u00b2)", "Chain link fence weaving (up to 20 ft height)", "Vinyl (PVC) coating of wire and fabric", "Single\u2011loop bale tie manufacturing", "High\u2011carbon wire drawing", "Security mesh (mini\u2011mesh) production", "Wire straightening and cutting", "Galvanized tension bar and rod manufacturing", "Fabricated panel production (gates, kennels, temporary panels)", "Agricultural wire production (vineyard, trellis, high\u2011tensile, electric fence)"], "industries": ["Chain link fence", "Industrial wire", "Recycling and baling wire", "High\u2011carbon wire", "Agricultural fencing", "Security and prison construction"], "materials": ["Low\u2011carbon steel (C1006\u2013C1026)", "High\u2011carbon steel (1027\u20131065)", "Galvanized steel", "Vinyl\u2011coated steel", "Black annealed wire"], "equipment": ["Wire galvanizing line", "Computer\u2011controlled chain link weaving machines", "Vinyl coating line", "Security mesh machines", "High\u2011carbon wire drawing equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Only mass\u2011production galvanized tension bar facility in the United States (since 1993)", "Class 5 galvanizing capability (2 oz./ft\u00b2) meeting ASTM A392 Class 2", "Three U.S. manufacturing facilities in Norman OK, Birmingham AL, and Sacramento CA", "Computer\u2011controlled chain link weaving machines producing fabric up to 20 ft tall", "All products melted and manufactured in the USA"], "facts_used": ["Founded March 1992 by Max Moore and Steve Peters -> /about-us", "Acquired Acme Fence and Iron equipment -> /about-us", "Installed state\u2011of\u2011the\u2011art galvanizing line -> /about-us", "Built only U.S. mass\u2011production galvanized tension bar facility in 1993 -> /about-us", "Added 30,000 sq. ft. facility and vinyl coating line in 1998 -> /about-us", "Operates three U.S. manufacturing facilities (Norman, Birmingham, Sacramento) -> /", "Main markets: industrial wire, recycling wire, high\u2011carbon wire, chain link fence -> /", "Products sold through expert distributors -> /", "Class 5 galvanizing capability meeting ASTM A392 Class 2 -> /about-us", "Security mesh machines for mini\u2011mesh up to 20 ft for prison/security -> /about-us", "Products melted and manufactured in the USA -> /about-us", "Headquarters: Norman, OK (P.O. Box CC) -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Southwestern Wire was started in March 1992 when Max Moore and Steve Peters acquired the machinery and equipment of Acme Fence and Iron from the Bank of Oklahoma.", "founded_year": "1992", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='southwestern-wire' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Space Age Electronics was founded in 1963 in Mt Holly, North Carolina. The company designs and manufactures code-compliant fire and life safety solutions tailored to system integrators, operating from ISO 9001 certified facilities in the United States. Over six decades, it has developed a brand family that includes the Infinity Series of modular components alongside integration accessories, surge protection, and building control.

