UPDATE companies SET description='Specialty Woodworks, Inc. is based in Lexington, South Carolina. The company began three decades ago as a small workshop providing basic woodworking services.

It now operates as an architectural woodworking and custom design firm, offering design, engineering, fabrication, and installation for millwork, doors, window casings, and historic restoration. The engineering team produces shop drawings from client designs or creates custom designs, integrating with CAD-to-production workflows and CNC precision cutting equipment. In-house capabilities include millwork fabrication, door and casing fabrication, and pre-construction services, allowing the firm to handle projects of any scope. The company''s precision-oriented equipment enables drilling, carving, and cutting materials to exacting standards without sacrificing quality.

The firm serves architects, designers, and general contractors who need high-end architectural woodwork for commercial and historic buildings. Its portfolio includes restoration, upfit, and repurposing projects, where in-house fabrication enables matching exacting historic specifications. Businesses seeking to preserve historic structures rather than demolish them are a noted client base.

Specialty Woodworks differentiates itself through uncompromising quality and craftsmanship, with installations meeting AWI quality standards. The company highlights its unlimited capabilities, pre-construction support, and a culture of pride in workmanship as reasons clients rely on them for complex architectural challenges.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Pre-Construction Services", "Engineering & Fabrication", "In-house Doors & Window Casing Fabrication", "In-house Millwork Fabrication", "CAD to Production Technology", "CNC Precision Cutting Technology", "Restoration", "Upfits", "Repurposing", "Installation", "Architectural woodworking", "Custom design", "Shop drawings", "Project management", "Historic replication", "Precision drilling, carving, cutting"], "industries": ["Historic preservation", "Commercial construction", "Architectural woodwork"], "materials": ["Wood", "Metal", "Stone"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house full fabrication capabilities for millwork, doors, and casings", "CAD-to-production workflow with CNC precision cutting", "Installation meeting AWI quality standards", "Expertise in historic restoration, upfits, and repurposing", "Pre-construction services and engineering support"], "facts_used": ["Lexington, South Carolina headquarters -> db", "Founded three decades ago as a small workshop -> db (capabilities)", "Architectural woodworking and custom design firm -> page /", "30 years of designing, crafting, and installing architectural solutions -> page /", "In-house doors & window casing fabrication -> db (capabilities)", "In-house millwork fabrication -> db (capabilities)", "CAD to production technology -> db (products)", "CNC precision cutting technology -> db (products)", "Pre-construction services -> db (capabilities)", "Engineering & fabrication -> db (capabilities)", "Restoration, upfits, repurposing expertise -> page /", "Installation meets AWI quality standards -> page /", "Works with architects, designers, contractors -> page /", "Materials: wood, metal, stone -> page /", "Family of people, pride in craftsmanship -> page /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our precision-oriented equipment enables the production team to drill, carve and cut materials for any size or scope of work with exacting standards.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='specialty-woodworks-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Spector Textile Products operates from a 50,000-square-foot facility in Lawrence, Massachusetts. The company has served industrial accounts across North America for more than 85 years and remains a family-owned and operated business. Established as a family enterprise, it has grown into a primary source for manufactured textile products.

The company specializes in custom manufacturing of textile products, including industrial-grade truck covers, laundry bags, and paper products for offices and construction trailers. Its diverse product line serves both small and large companies, with an emphasis on short-run and custom orders. Custom printing of logos on laundromat products is a core service. Production and inventory are managed from its 50,000-square-foot Lawrence facility, enabling immediate delivery on many items.

Spector supplies paint and hardware stores, construction firms, laundry and dry-cleaning businesses, medical facilities, industrial uniform providers, and moving-supply companies throughout North America.

