UPDATE companies SET description='Spectrum Plastics Group, a DuPont business, operates its flagship packaging manufacturing facility in Pleasant Prairie, Wisconsin. The 161,000-square-foot site runs 35 extrusion lines around the clock and holds an ISO Class 7 cleanroom. The company traces its roots to PPC Industries, Inc., doing business as Spectrum Plastics Group, and became part of DuPont''s portfolio.

The facility specializes in blown film extrusion, producing commodity and specialty poly bags, converted pouches, and monolayer and coextruded films. Capabilities extend to concept development, quick-turn prototyping, regulatory support, and manufacturing transfer programs.

Spectrum serves medical device OEMs across cardiovascular, structural heart, neurovascular, electrophysiology, orthopedics, robotic surgery, fluid management, gastrointestinal, pharmaceutical, urology, ophthalmology, trauma care, and diagnostics markets. It also supplies industrial and defense sectors, food packaging, and drug delivery device manufacturers. The component webstore provides off-the-shelf tubing and components for rapid procurement.

The company emphasizes its six-sigma-level extrusion of acetal core mandrels, on-site same-day testing and revision, and a full-service model that spans design through scalable production. Its quality system is certified to ISO 9001:2015, ISO 13485:2016, and ISO FSSC 22000, with CE marking for European market access.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 13485:2016','ISO FSSC22000','CE Mark']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Blown Film Extrusion", "Microbore Extrusion", "Silicone Extrusion", "Injection Molding", "Quick-Turn Molding", "Precision Machining", "Machining & Fabrication", "Laser Processing", "Finishing Services & Assembly", "Sub-Assembly & Assembly Manufacturing", "Quick-Turn Prototyping", "Concept Development", "Regulatory Services", "Manufacturing Transfers", "Quality Management Support", "Design & Development", "Catheter Technologies", "Medical Balloon Manufacturing", "Flexible Packaging & Film Production", "Extruded Medical Tubing", "Converting", "Fabrication/Secondary Operations"], "industries": ["Medical Packaging", "Extruded Medical Tubing", "Medical Balloons", "Industrial / Defense", "Neuromodulation Medical Devices & Components", "Cardiovascular", "Structural Heart", "Neurovascular", "Electrophysiology", "Orthopedics / Sports Medicine", "MIS / Robotic Surgery", "Fluid Management", "GI / Enteral Feeding", "Pharmaceutical / BioPharma", "Urology", "Ophthalmology", "Trauma / Wound Care", "Diagnostics", "Food Packaging", "Drug Delivery Devices"], "materials": ["Acetal", "Silicone", "Polyethylene"], "equipment": ["35 Extrusion lines"], "volume": "Low to mid-volume production; high-volume Class 101 multicavity molds", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["35 extrusion lines operating 24/7", "ISO Class 7 cleanroom for medical packaging", "Six Sigma quality on acetal core mandrel extrusion", "Quick-turn prototyping and molding with same-day testing", "Full-service model from concept development to scalable production"], "facts_used": 