UPDATE companies SET description='Speed Systems Inc was founded in 1970 in Brookfield, Wisconsin. The company operates a manufacturing facility in Brookfield where it designs and builds tools for the electrical utility industry.

The company produces hand- and drill-operated tools, adjustable tools that eliminate the need for bushings, and specialized equipment for preparing primary and secondary cable for termination and for installing cable system components. It also offers custom tool design, developing wrenches and other tools based on direct input from linemen. All products are manufactured at the Brookfield facility.

Speed Systems serves the electrical utility sector, selling through authorized distributors in the United States, Canada, and internationally. Manufacturer representatives are located across the U.S. to support local needs.

The company emphasizes safety, efficiency, ergonomics, and value in its designs. It highlights fast lead times and a responsive custom-tool process as key differentiators, with the goal of meeting specific field requirements.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom tool design", "Manufacturing of hand and drill-operated tools", "Cable preparation for termination", "Cable system component installation", "Adjustable tool manufacturing (bushing-free)"], "industries": ["Electrical utility", "Power cable installation"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Unparalleled lead times", "Custom tools designed from linemen input", "Manufacturer representatives across the U.S.", "Products designed and built in Brookfield, WI facility", "Focus on safety, efficiency, ergonomics, and value"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1970 -> db", "Founded 1970 -> /", "Headquarters Brookfield, WI -> db", "Headquarters Brookfield, WI -> /", "Manufacturing facility in Brookfield, WI -> /", "Products: hand and drill-operated tools, adjustable tools without bushings -> /", "Custom tool design based on linemen input -> /", "Manufacturer reps across U.S. -> /", "Authorized distributors in U.S., Canada, worldwide -> /", "Focus on safety, efficiency, ergonomics, value -> /", "Speedy delivery / unparalleled lead times -> /", "American Made Since 1970 -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Speed Systems has been manufacturing quality, field-tested products for over 50 years. Our tools are designed and built in our manufacturing facility in Brookfield, WI.", "founded_year": "1970", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='speed-systems-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Split Mountain Metals was founded in 2014 by Brad and Carley Brenteson in Belgrade, Montana. Brad Brenteson brought a lifetime of metalworking experience, from growing up on a farm in north-central Montana to formal training as a machinist and welder in Helena. The couple established the shop to provide architectural steel fabrication for high-end residential projects across the state.

The company produces custom steel stairs, railings and guards, fireplace surrounds and cladding, exposed structural steel such as trusses and knife plates, steel-fin screens and gates, and chimney caps in raw steel, Corten, or stainless. Every project begins with a detailed consultation and design approval before any material is cut; all layout, cutting, welding, and finishing is performed in the Belgrade facility.

Split Mountain Metals works directly with architects, interior designers, and high-end residential builders who require precision fabrication for exceptional homes. Their work appears in projects throughout Montana, including floating stairs, horizontal-bar railings, blackened-steel fireplace surrounds, and exposed steel trusses for luxury residences.

