UPDATE companies SET description='Summers Manufacturing, Inc. is based in Devils Lake, North Dakota. The company traces its roots to 1965 when Harley Summers purchased patent rights for Goebel truck and pickup hoists and began production in a small shop in Maddock, ND. He incorporated the business as Summers Manufacturing Company, Inc. in 1969. In 2007, the company became 100 percent employee-owned through an Employee Stock Ownership Plan (ESOP).

The company designs and manufactures a range of agricultural equipment, including tillage tools (vertical tillage, variable-rate tillage, disk rippers, chisel plows, harrows, and rolling choppers), land rollers (coil packers, hydraulic-fold and trail-type Super Rollers), application equipment (Spray Fill Xpress sprayer fill systems, grain handling conveyors, and field belts), mounted attachments (harrows, rolling baskets, rolling choppers), and rock pickers. Production takes place at its Devils Lake campus, which includes a 26,000-square-foot factory built in 1980 and expanded multiple times through 2010, and an Aberdeen, South Dakota facility added in 2013 for assembly, parts, and distribution.

The company collaborates with research and technology partners such as Grand Farm (Fargo, ND), AgRevival (Gibbon, MN), PTI (Pontiac, IL), and Mach to develop variable-rate tillage and precision agriculture solutions.

The company emphasizes field-tested durability, citing its 2000 introduction of the industry''s first true vertical tillage tool (the Supercoulter) and a 10-year limited warranty on select land roller models launched in 2018. Its stated mission is to build field-tested tough equipment that helps farmers feed and fuel the world.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Agricultural equipment manufacturing", "Welding and fabrication", "Paint finishing", "Assembly", "Parts distribution", "Field service and support"], "industries": ["Agriculture", "Farming", "Agricultural equipment"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Super Coulter Samurai", "VRT Renegade", "Spray Fill Xpress", "Super Roller (Coil Packer, Hydraulic Fold, Trail Type)", "3RT Tillage Platform", "Disk Ripper", "Elite Chisel", "Chisel Plow", "Harrow Packer", "Rolling Chopper", "Mounted Rolling Basket", "Rock Picker", "1648 Field Belt"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Industry''s first true vertical tillage tool (Supercoulter, 2000)", "10-year limited warranty on select land roller models (2018)", "Variable-rate tillage adjustable on the fly via iPad (VRT Renegade, 2018)", "100% employee-owned through ESOP since 2007", "Spray Fill Xpress system cuts sprayer refill time (2015)"], "facts_used": ["Founding year 1965 -> /about-us", "Founder Harley Summers -> /about-us", "Incorporation 1969 -> /about-us", "Employee-owned ESOP 2007 -> /about-us", "Headquarters Devils Lake, ND -> db, /about-us", "Facility sizes and expansions -> /about-us", "Aberdeen facility 2013 -> /about-us", "Product lines (tillage, land rollers, application, mounted attachments, rock pickers) -> /, /about-us", "Industry focus agriculture -> /about-us", "Mission statement -> /about-us", "First vertical tillage tool Supercoulter 2000 -> /about-us", "10-year warranty on land rollers 2018 -> /about-us", "Variable-rate tillage via iPad 2018 -> /about-us", "Spray Fill Xpress 2015 -> /about-us", "Part