UPDATE companies SET description='For nearly four decades, T&L Muumuu Factory has carried on the tradition of garment making in Honolulu, Hawaii. The family-owned and operated business began as a small local shop and grew through word of mouth and lasting customer relationships. Today, the company continues to design, cut, and sew every piece in its Honolulu workshop, using original patterns that have guided generations of makers.

The product line centers on women''s muumuus, aloha shirts sized up to 4X, and a children''s collection of keiki tops, skirts, and dresses for both performance and everyday wear. Each garment is handcrafted in Hawaii, with the workshop handling design, pattern making, cutting, and sewing under one roof. The factory also offers alteration services, including same-day turnaround for retail customers.

The company specializes in custom orders, providing a streamlined communication process for bulk and made-to-measure requests. Free domestic shipping is available on orders over $200.

By preserving original patterns and maintaining hands-on production, T&L Muumuu Factory aims to support and perpetuate the cultural traditions behind Hawaiian garments, delivering each piece from their hands to the customer with the same attention that started it all.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design", "Cutting", "Sewing", "Custom garment manufacturing", "Pattern making", "Alterations"], "industries": ["Apparel", "Hawaiian wear", "Hula wear", "Custom clothing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family owned and operated", "Handcrafted in Hawai\u02bbi", "Locally designed and produced", "Custom orders for h\u0101lau and groups", "Original patterns used for generations"], "facts_used": ["Located in Honolulu, Hawaii -> /", "Family owned and operated -> /", "Nearly forty years of garment making tradition -> /", "Designs, cuts, and sews in own workshop -> /", "Uses original patterns passed down generations -> /", "Products: muumuus, aloha shirts, keiki wear -> /", "Specializes in custom orders for h\u0101lau and groups -> /", "Offers same-day alterations -> /", "Free domestic shipping on orders over $200 -> /", "Ships internationally (Japan, Mexico) -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Each piece is designed, cut, and sewn in our workshop.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='t-l-muumuu-factory' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='T&R Tooling, LLC operates from a 40,000-square-foot facility in Valley View, Texas. The company was founded by Tom and Ronney, two toolmakers who began with a small backyard shop in nearby Krum. Their partnership grew from a handshake and a shared belief that they could better serve customers together. The business remains family-owned.

The shop provides end-to-end plastic injection molding and custom tooling. Services span mold design and construction (both in-house and offshore), mold repair, optimization, and transfer, as well as low- to high-volume injection molding. Prototyping capabilities include 3D printing and CNC machining. Post-molding operations cover first-article inspection, assembly, packaging, hot-stamping, and inventory stocking programs. The facility houses 14 injection molding machines, eight machining centers, and an assembly department, supported by SolidWorks, Mastercam, and Fusion 360.

Customers come from aerospace, automotive, robotics, and other industrial sectors. Named references include Pinnacle Safety Products (safety equipment), North Texas Plastics, and Displays by Martin Paul, Inc. (display manufacturing).

